Perf
  - Add a bounded cross-page bitmap LRU for raster tiles. Not “keep page alive”, just retain maybe the last N                                                                       
    decoded tiles or last selected map bundle. This directly attacks PLATE -> CHART reload without preserving                                                                       
    whole UI state.                          
  - Limit concurrent zip reads/decode to a sane number. Current full-batch parallelism improved crispness but   
    may create zip/file contention. A dispatcher/semaphore around reads may reduce worst-case wall time.                                                                            
  - Prefetch on PLATE page after leaving CHART. If memory budget allows bytes but not bitmaps, retain                                                                               
    compressed tile bytes or warm zip entries for the likely return viewport.             
  - Reduce planned Android raster count if density/viewport math is over-eager. This is the first thing I’d                                                                         
    measure next, because 96 vs 22 is a much bigger gap than 300ms vs 200ms.              



